# Qt 6.7.3 owns and deletes the GUI paint pool during QCoreApplication teardown.
# Its Unix QThread::wait() can finish before destroy_current_thread_data()
# releases the pthread's reference. The reported loss is consistent with this
# process-exit race. This definite new allocation needs its own suppression.
# Restrict it to the observed Qt Fusion scrollbar gradient-fill call chain;
# application-created threads and other definite leaks must remain visible.
{
   Qt Fusion scrollbar paint worker data - shutdown leak
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:_Znwm
